# L §4.4's list (tally 2.3, #247; S4, C7): an ask line's `law` or `as known` asks for one day, so a window there is
# the hole naming it, the line's own (`the law of an ask`, `as known`). Before: REFCORE-NOT-YET (HoleSignal).
=== m.tally
model hd4
  tally 2
  on 2026-04-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
source card "invented"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input w: date
input wide: date
input rate: num
input apr: month
input d2: date
input n5: int
input mrate[m in months]: num
input drate[d in days]: num
def r_at: num = rate at w
def r_wide: num = rate at wide
def r_reader: num = rate at reader
def held: date = w
version v_card
  cite card
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  w = window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-03) "c"
  wide = window(2026-04-20, 2026-05-10) "c"
  opening[konto] = 500.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "c"
  mrate[*] = 2 "c"
  apr = 2026-04 "c"
  d2 = 2026-04-02 "c"
  n5 = 5 "c"
  drate[*] = 3 "c"
version r1
  cite card
  governs ..2026-04
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 1 "c"
version r2
  cite card
  governs 2026-05..
  known 2026-01-01
  rate = 5 "c"
ask a_law: r_reader law w
ask a_law_wide: r_reader law wide
ask a_known2: bal(konto, d2) as known w
=== expect
a_known2: ?"date within window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-03) not precise enough for as known" (w)
a_law: ?"date within window(2026-04-01, 2026-04-03) not precise enough for the law of an ask" (w)
a_law_wide: ?"date within window(2026-04-20, 2026-05-10) not precise enough for the law of an ask" (wide)
warning: WARN-UNREAD def held is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD def r_at is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD def r_wide is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input apr is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input drate is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input mrate is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input n5 is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD place world is read by nothing
